ID: vr-45
Title: One session manager, isolated heads and independent feature colors

Status: DONE
Milestone: One GUI controls all six authored variants and multiple named speaking heads.
Dependencies: vr-37, vr-38, vr-40, vr-43, vr-44

Purpose:
Two explicitly opted-in local chats need separate heads, models, audio owners
and identifying colors, without asking the owner to run different launchers.

Tasks:
[x] Independent mesh/eye/hair/lip/eyebrow pickers and hex in supported renderers.
[x] Named CLI hosts select all six variants and accept live validated colors.
[x] One manager GUI creates, lists, configures, speaks through and closes heads.
[x] Show each session's model, confirmed colors and native controls; no transcript logs.
[x] Preserve per-head capability, RAM speech, cancellation and isolated mutable resources.
[x] Correct the observed Windows Ctrl+C hang in the native MPFB console.
[x] Qualify concurrent sessions, renderer changes, errors, lifecycle and actual GUI.
[x] Update chapter/guide/index/ledger, issue/Project, verified source and owned continuity.

Acceptance criteria:
Normal launch opens the single manager. It can create two distinct simultaneous
heads with independent models/colors and address each by session name.
Settings change without neural regeneration; renderer errors are visible.
No head/model or color is silently substituted. Legacy originals remain.
GUI controls represent actual native controls, including applicability limits.
One session's Stop/Close does not stop another. Manager Exit closes only its
owned heads. Existing external CLI sessions stay independent unless explicitly
selected for Close. Cold setup and per-head CPU/RAM costs remain explicit.
No camera/microphone activation, cloud speech, automatic download, transcript
persistence, automatic agent hooks, release, deployment or accuracy acceptance.

